Patch-Source: https://github.com/freeunitorg/freeunit/issues/665
Router fix for a request claimed by a worker that dies before
REQ_HEADERS_ACK (v2, not committed upstream yet).

diff --git a/CHANGES b/CHANGES
index 368f6745..ab7f7204 100644
--- a/CHANGES
+++ b/CHANGES
@@ -18,6 +18,14 @@ Changes with FreeUnit 1.37.2                                     31 Oct 2026
        memory error, released an njs VM that was never compiled and crashed
        the router.
 
+    *) Bugfix: a request that a worker took from the queue of its
+       application and did not acknowledge before it died was never
+       answered without "limits": {"timeout"}. It also kept the application
+       and its listener, so a later configuration on the same port failed
+       with "Address already in use". The router now answers such a request
+       with 503: at once if no worker claimed it, and 5 seconds after the
+       exit if a worker claimed it.
+
     *) Feature: the PHP module now builds with PHP 8.7, which removed five
        members of "sapi_module_struct". The module names the members that it
        sets, so a member that PHP removes no longer shifts the others.
